WEBVTT

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.660
Do you know which major league team

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.010
Out!

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.090
the Nashville Bulls are affiliated with?

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.330
No!

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.830
Do you know how many teams exist in the minors?

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.580
The Chicago Bisons.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.750
Bisons?!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.880
Isn't the Bisons where Gibson was playing—

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.390
G-Gibson?!

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.640
Wh-What's he doing there?

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.650
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.650
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:52.940
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:52.940
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.320
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.320
the only thing I truly have

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.620
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.620
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:08.960
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:08.960
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.220
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.220
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.600
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.600
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.690
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.690
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:31.230
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:31.230
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.320
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.320
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.620
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.620
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:46.870
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:46.910
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:52.550
namida kareru made

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:52.550
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:57.590
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:57.590
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:02.930
namida hareru made

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:02.930
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.940
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.940
though I may lose my way,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.770
egakikake no ima

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.770
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.270
kizamu

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:19.030
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.570
akashi

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:19.030
kono te de

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.790
Fully Back on the Mound

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.790
Fully Back on the Mound

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.130
What's going on?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:38.170
Didn't that old guy retire more than a month ago?

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.300
No, they just treated it as a retirement in his contract.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.270
It was his request, so that he could start over from scratch.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:54.430
Just yesterday, he passed the Bisons tryouts,

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:59.320
signed a new contract for the AA Bulls, and here he is.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.080
No, wait. I still don't get it.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.520
I don't care how he got here.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:08.000
What is he thinking by starting from scratch after all these years?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.400
He's already reached the top,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.420
so why would a guy in his forties risk his health

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.420
Play!

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.340
just to start all over again?

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.350
Strike!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.960
97 mph?

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.720
Just a month ago...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.310
No, that one's even faster than in the World Cup.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:37.300
Gibson completely retrained his body over the past two months.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:42.240
When he was confident in his pitching and was accepted into the minors,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.310
he gave me a call.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:49.760
He asked me to tell you guys to come watch this game.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.750
Us guys?

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.530
W-Wait a minute!

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.600
Why would Gibson tell you something like that?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.180
I guess it's time I told you.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:10.010
It wasn't mere coincidence that you came to me for treatment.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.850
The one who recommended me to the Hornets' management

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.370
was none other than Gibson.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.270
Strike out!

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.150
Wh-What do you mean?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.070
What's your relationship with him anyway?

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:31.040
Gibson is a former patient of mine.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.110
Ten years ago,

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:39.000
he returned from Japan and had switched gears to get back into the majors, but...

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:44.130
His heart had been crushed more seriously than he could ever have anticipated.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.970
His family died in an accident.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:55.390
Yeah, I heard he went back to America hoping to mend Junior's broken heart.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.440
Yeah.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:57.780
But...

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.110
It wasn't just Junior's heart that shattered.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.850
Gibson took a baseball player's life in Japan,

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.420
so he devoted himself to Japanese baseball to repent,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.830
only to end up losing his own family.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:21.350
Despite all the pain, he kept fighting and dedicated himself to preparing for the upcoming baseball season,

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:23.210
but he burned himself out.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.860
Back then, I was the team psychiatrist for the San Francisco Guardians.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.770
"For my son, and for Honda Jr. in Japan,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.930
I must keep fighting on the mound."

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.690
That was all he could think about,

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:46.490
and I was too young to be able to do anything more for him than what I had learned from textbooks.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.910
He couldn't even play well in the exhibition games,

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.530
so he had become irritated and careless.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.120
But then one day, there was an incident.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.300
Hey, he's here!

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.710
Hey, Gibson!

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.330
Sign this, please!

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.260
Wow, he just ignored us.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.470
What's his problem?

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.050
Then...

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:17.560
There was a little boy who had snuck in to ask Gibson for an autograph.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:24.610
Gibson had never been the type to turn down a little boy's wish.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.570
How'd you get in here?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.320
This place is off-limits.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.530
If you want an autograph, follow the rules.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.530
Hey, kid.

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:43.470
You shouldn't be here.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.200
Now, come with me.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:51.670
Mister!

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:52.780
Please, wait!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.530
Hey, stop walking!

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.060
That was a dick move.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.350
That was a dick move, Mister!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:06.030
Even if you're in a bad mood, you went way too far.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:11.340
That kid just wanted an autograph from his hero!

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.510
Who do you think you are?!

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:16.220
Are you lecturing me?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.480
Rules are rules.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:18.450
Age doesn't matter!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.210
If I let one person break the rules, I'd have to sign autographs for everyone in the world!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.550
Go apologize to him right now and give him your autograph!

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:32.220
I know you're still in a lot of pain,

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:40.580
and I'm really sorry that I can't get rid of the darkness in your heart

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.190
that makes you hate God himself,

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:43.570
but...

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:48.170
If you can't help being an asshole to your friends,

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.920
you should just quit baseball!

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:56.700
Nobody wants to see you play baseball like this.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:02.510
Not your son, not the boy in Japan, not that little boy, or any of your other fans!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:06.920
If you've even forgotten your duty of being a role model for your fans,

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.450
then you're not qualified to be a professional athlete!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.720
Hey, hold on!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.310
Sorry, boy.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.260
After that incident, Gibson began to change.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.170
He buried his pain deep inside of himself,

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:07.270
and focused only on his pitching when he was on the mound.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:14.540
He got his game back and pitched a no-hitter in the season opener.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.570
And in the summer All-Star Game,

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.810
he got six consecutive strike outs.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:25.660
You were in the crowd watching as a grade schooler, right?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.960
Yeah.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:33.970
Out!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.890
Until then,

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.700
he was pitching with a sense of duty for his family and Honda Shigeharu.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:49.000
For him, baseball had become a means of repentance.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.070
However,

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:57.950
when he was at his lowest, he thought about his reasons for playing baseball,

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:01.410
and the answer was simple.

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.710
He'd play for himself, because he loves baseball,

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:12.040
and for baseball fans everywhere, because they also love baseball.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.970
It was his dream to keep standing on the mound until his body stopped moving.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.510
Strike!

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:26.000
Gibson was worried about both you and Junior.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:34.360
You both fear being demoted or making tiny mistakes and have lost track of your goals.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:41.250
"Why are the two young prodigies who left the crowd in awe at the World Cup

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.990
having trouble settling down as major leaguers?"

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.020
He was truly infuriated.

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:51.230
What's wrong with striking out?

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.050
What's wrong with giving up home runs?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.850
What's wrong with falling?

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.630
You just have to get back up.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:02.290
He was hoping for you two to grow to be amazing baseball players,

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:06.550
and be heroes to many fans.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.480
There's another thing he told me.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:14.900
"I can't retire after betraying the Chicago fans' hopes."

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.250
"I must return to the majors as soon as I can,

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:21.360
break my record of 101 mph, and make the crowds go wild."

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.120
Strike out!

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:39.000
I see.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:39.970
He went back.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.100
Yes.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.390
He's probably on the plane by now.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.370
I'm sure Junior was in the crowd too.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.060
I passed on your message.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.230
Did Goro say anything?

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.710
No, nothing in particular.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:00.280
But I'm sure he gained something.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.630
Hey, Miss, beer and a hot dog.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.550
$10.50.

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:22.110
Are you serious?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.970
The price goes up every time I come here.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.030
Goodness, Dear!

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:26.410
We can do this later.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:27.930
The game's about to start.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:31.420
Well, my game doesn't start without these!

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:36.540
Today's the day! We're back with the start of the second half of the season.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.950
44 wins and 46 losses.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.440
The Hornets concluded the first half with two net losses, ranking third in their division.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:47.700
This will be a three-game series against the Minnesota Coyotes, who lead the division with six more wins than the Hornets.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.030
Today is the crucial first game of the series.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.830
We expected that they'd start out with their ace, Rosario, today,

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:58.160
but they've kept the rotation regardless of the All-Star break and have brought out Shigeno.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:04.780
The Coyotes, on the other hand, will face the Hornets with five batters above a .300 batting average.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:08.940
They'll also have the fourth batter, Silva, who has been superb since his recovery

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:11.600
and has become the driving force in maintaining the Coyotes' division lead.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.920
The way you've been pitching lately, you don't stand a chance against us.

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.440
We're taking this game.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.880
We can't lose this one if we want to get to the top.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:33.370
Shouldn't we have used Rosario?

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:36.140
Now hitting, number 1: Strawberry!

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:36.140
Hey, Dear!

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:37.570
Over here!

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.060
Come on, hurry!

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:43.710
Just in time.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:45.760
Hey, look.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.250
Look who's starting.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.550
It's Shigeno!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.470
Play ball!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.120
Ball!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.620
Ball four!

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.740
No outs with runners on first and second?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.790
What is he thinking?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.670
What are you doing, Shigeno?

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:23.710
I'm gracing you with my presence, so pitch like you mean it!

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:29.010
Ball!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:31.820
Ball!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.180
No, wait a minute.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.270
Isn't that...

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.510
Yeah.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:41.940
The crowd hasn't noticed, but...

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:45.840
Ball!

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:46.900
Ball three!

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:49.130
That idiot!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.670
Go back to the Bats and start over!

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.720
N-No, wait.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.590
Look at that.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.840
Boss, look at Shigeno's speed!

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:03.830
Yeah.

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.890
But he hasn't pitched any strikes.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:10.510
Ball!

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.950
Ball four!

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.510
Bases loaded!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.350
Three walks and the bases are loaded!

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.310
Silva steps up to the plate with no outs and the bases loaded!

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:22.450
Time out!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.580
Get out, you berserk pitcher!

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:29.320
It's time to quit if you're too scared to pitch in the strike zone!

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.250
Shut up!

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:32.950
He hasn't given up a run yet!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.160
Stop crying like a baby and cheer him on!

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.300
What happened?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.420
Your speed.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.970
You haven't pitched at 100 mph since the opening game.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:46.420
Oh, was that 100 mph?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.440
I didn't notice.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:54.010
But that doesn't matter if you can't throw a single strike.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:57.680
If you can't control it, throw a forkball or something.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.290
Let's get some strikes.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:15:59.930
No.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.170
I'll stick with my fastballs.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:09.230
We can't strike Silva out with breaking balls, and they're pointless to begin with.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:14.410
Besides, even if we hold him down with passive pitching, the crowd won't be entertained.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:20.910
Whatever suits you best.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:24.850
It doesn't look like he was afraid of pitching strikes.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:26.080
Yeah.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.420
Play!

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:34.300
Wake up, Shigeno.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:39.620
Even if you fall, just get back up every time.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.300
Grow to be a true super star athlete

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:49.900
and continue to be every fan's hero.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.040
Strike!

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:04.460
B-Bastard...

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:10.000
He's completely changed since the last time I faced him.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:18.680
This is it.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:22.770
This is your real pitching that I saw in the World Cup!

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.980
Let's go, Shigeno!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.900
Unless I can hit your real pitches,

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:37.360
I still owe you for the World Cup!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.230
Strike out!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.670
All right, Shigeno!

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.090
Is he... back?

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.960
Yeah, no doubt about it.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.270
He's definitely back.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.820
He's pitching boldly with the bases loaded.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:10.350
And the sight of him picking up his cap...

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:15.400
If that's not the real Shigeno, then I don't know what is!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.820
Shigeno!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.240
You're back.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.250
Geez...

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:22.830
He's finally come out of a long, long tunnel.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.500
That is, of course, if he's not just wearing a bigger cap.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:32.190
Being a hero, huh?

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.390
That's right.

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.010
It's always been my dream.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:47.570
The players I watched from the stands were always blindingly radiant.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:54.270
Now that you've become a professional, you're not just pitching for yourself anymore.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.200
Strike out!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.070
All right!

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:05.490
What was I doing worrying about motivation and goals?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:12.920
I don't know any of their faces or names, but I'm standing on this stage made of their dreams,

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:15.920
shouldering every baseball fanatic's love for baseball.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.100
Strike out!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.660
Strike out!

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:30.920
After loading the bases, he struck out the fourth, fifth, and the sixth batters!

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:34.480
Shigeno breaks through a pinch with amazing pitching!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.580
That's great.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.540
It's the fruit of your efforts.

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:41.850
No.

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.770
I didn't do anything.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.260
He did it himself

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.790
with his strong passion for baseball.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.840
102 mph?

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.380
Facing fast pitchers is always thrilling.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.720
Next time...

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.970
In my next at-bat, I'll hit his pitch.

00:20:26.480 --> 00:20:28.120
You'll pitch the last inning too?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.830
But you've already thrown 130 pitches.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.320
Let's leave this one to Watts.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.420
No, I insist.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:42.520
I need to show all the Hornets fans today that <i>this</i>...

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:44.580
is the real Goro Shigeno.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.170
Out!

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:05.490
Game over!

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.370
In the first game of the second half of the season against the Coyotes,

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.080
Shigeno hit three for three <i>and</i> shut out the Coyotes!

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:14.480
Well, look at that.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.870
I bet I'm too unreliable for him.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.100
He's definitely back.

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:20.800
Yeah.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.910
Bravo!

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:27.180
I'll have you make me a lot of profit after investing in your treatment.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.140
I hate that bastard.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.780
But it's not over yet.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:37.020
The Coyotes will ultimately take the title.

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:39.290
That was wonderful pitching today.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.360
What was different?

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.540
Oh, my fastball, I guess.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:45.950
I was feeling good about my fastballs, so I focused on...

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.950
Great job, Shigeno!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.240
You've got my cheering to thank!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.130
Isn't that guy...

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:53.760
You made this a great start to the second half of the season.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.520
We hope to see more from you.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:56.970
Oh, thanks.

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:00.260
Hey, Shigeno!

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.020
Give me your autograph!

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:07.540
Don't be so cold!

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:10.470
Are you still mad about what happened on the bus?

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.440
Dear!

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:27.570
That's the game-winning ball!

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:32.940
I'll be back, Shigeno!

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:35.160
You better take the title!

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:58.890
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:58.890
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:04.270
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:04.270
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:10.530
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:10.530
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:15.330
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:15.330
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:21.960
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:21.960
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:27.800
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:27.800
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:33.640
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:33.640
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:39.060
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:39.060
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:45.520
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:45.520
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:50.780
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:54.240
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:54.240
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:56.700
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.240 --> 00:24:03.080
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:03.080
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:06.920
sotto

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:06.920
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:15.090
Preview

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:15.090
Preview

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:13.090
You're ditching club activities and you have multiple jobs?

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:15.970
Don't tell me you're going to quit softball...

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:17.100
You better be kidding me!

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:18.900
Come to your senses, Shimizu!

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:21.140
That's not the you I know!

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:23.770
Next time, on Major: Each Person's Summer.

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:27.040
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:29.270
Next Time

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:29.270
Next Time

